      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Unity already does this by default, it's called mipmaps and it helps to prevent jagged or sparkly textures at a distance. It doesn't save any graphics memory though unless you were to use streaming mipmaps, but we're not doing that because unity's implementation of streaming mipmaps is too limited and not ideal for VRChat's use case.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-11-04T04:29:53.693Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Would be amazing if the VRC SDK would upload an avatar's textures at several different sizes. This way different resolutions of textures could be swapped out depending on how close the avatar is to you. If I'm not entirely wrong this could drastically reduce the amount of graphics memory in use, which is the biggest limitation of in-game performance. You rarely need the full-res avatar textures unless you yourself are wearing the avatar or you are right up close to it.\nI'm not a graphics expert so if this is nonsense I totally understand.",
